  "tools_practical_notes": {
    "purpose": "Operational knowledge gained during ai-adapter implementation (2026-10-11), supplementing tools_type_matrix with failure modes and conversion semantics.",
    "entries": [
      {
        "platform": "VS Code / Copilot",
        "artifact_kind": "agent",
        "yaml_type": "array",
        "operational_notes": [
          "Object-format tools does not merely drop the tools field: VS Code fails to load the entire custom agent, and it never appears in the agents dropdown.",
          "Agents with no tools key load fine; only object-format tools breaks loading.",
          "Tool names are VS Code built-ins (read, edit, search, execute, browser, web, todo, agent, vscode*, vscodeGeneral/*, vscodeNotebooks/*) or MCP '<server>/*'.",
          "Unknown tool names are ignored per official docs, so cross-platform names degrade silently rather than failing."
        ],
        "observed_case": "routeflags/japan-cannabinoid-trends .github/agents: 6 agents with object-format tools were invisible in VS Code; converting tools to array restored loading. The only working agent had no tools key at all."
      },
      {
        "platform": "OpenCode",
        "artifact_kind": "agent",
        "yaml_type": "object",
        "operational_notes": [
          "tools is deprecated in favor of permission (allow / ask / deny).",
          "Legacy semantics: true == {\"*\": \"allow\"}, false == {\"*\": \"deny\"}.",
          "Falsy entries (false) are meaningful in OpenCode (deny) but are dropped when converting to VS Code/Gemini array format, where presence-only is the semantics.",
          "Wildcard keys are supported in legacy tools (e.g. disable all tools of an MCP server)."
        ]
      },
      {
        "platform": "Gemini CLI",
        "artifact_kind": "agent",
        "yaml_type": "array",
        "operational_notes": [
          "Omitted tools inherits all tools from the parent session; an empty array is therefore a meaningful restriction, not an equivalent of omission.",
          "Wildcards: '*' (all tools), 'mcp_*' (all MCP tools), 'mcp_<server>_*' (one server).",
          "The name key must be a lowercase slug ([a-z0-9_-]); display names must be slugified at conversion time."
        ]
      },
      {
        "platform": "Claude Code",
        "artifact_kind": "agent",
        "yaml_type": "string",
        "operational_notes": [
          "Comma-separated tool names, e.g. 'Read, Grep, Glob, Bash'.",
          "Both array and object formats are invalid for Claude Code agents.",
          "Tool names follow Claude Code's own naming (Read, Grep, Glob, Bash, ...), not VS Code names."
        ]
      }
    ],
    "ai_adapter_mapping": {
      "canonical_store_format": "array — .github/agents/ is VS Code's native directory, so the store normalises to the VS Code shape",
      "validation": "agent_format.validate_agent_file(path, target_format='array'|'object'|'string') — one function, three platform expectations",
      "conversions": {
        "object_to_array": "agent_format.convert_agent_file_to_array (VS Code; falsy entries dropped)",
        "array_to_object": "agent_format.convert_agent_file (OpenCode; false entries preserved as deny)",
        "to_comma_string": "agent_format.convert_agent_file_to_string (Claude Code; accepts array or object input)"
      },
      "cli": [
        "sub-agent add/get/get-all --fix: object -> array for the standard (.github/agents/) path",
        "sub-agent get --format opencode --fix: array -> object",
        "sub-agent get --format claude: comma-separated string conversion at deploy time (never touches the store)",
        "sub-agent get --format codex: tools dropped entirely (Codex custom-agent TOML has no tools key; capability is governed by sandbox_mode)",
        "sub-agent get --format gemini: tools converted to array at deploy time"
      ],
      "shared_directory_caveat": ".github/agents/ is read by VS Code (array) and, via the .opencode symlink, by OpenCode (object). The two expectations are irreconcilable in one file; ai-adapter treats VS Code as canonical for that directory and deploys the OpenCode shape only via --format opencode."
    }
  },
